laurel 2974: larger GPU pool and larger kernel RAM on the 6 GB Mi A3; kept buffers give way before a pool request fails. Log 2026-11-03 02:54:49-02:55:00: `GPU pool 0 of 512 MB free`, 91-119 MB kept, 3-7 submissions in 5 s. New map (Mu 0101, mkadt.py): GPU pool 0x80000000 + 1 GiB (was 0xC0000000 + 512 MiB), TopazModem pool 0xC0000000 + 16 MiB (was 0xE0000000), kernel window 0xC1004000 + 3904 MiB to 0x1B5004000 (was 0xE1004000 + 3264 MiB; 1007 MiB below 4 GiB, was 495). GPU_POOL_MAX, the chunk table and lgp's unit table were already sized for 1 GiB. Self-checks: lgp_place (laurel_gpu_pool_core.h, host test) cuts a reserved range in front of kernel RAM or the modem pool; at the first allocation every chunk above 512 MiB must map and hold a pattern, the first that does not ends the pool, so a failure leaves 512 MiB (kill switch gpu_poolbig=0); 2100: a window past the ADT banks falls back to 3264 MiB (kill switch laurelramgrow=0). Pool pressure: keep() no longer keeps a pool buffer when under 64 MiB of the pool is free; redwood_gpu_pool_take gives kept pool buffers back, the oldest first, when the pool has no room: the window server's own request and pass-through take from all clients, other clients and IOSurfaces only from clients that are not the window server. Lines: `LAUREL GPU POOL: on: 1024 MiB at 0x80000000, 16 chunks of 64 MiB` or `LAUREL GPU POOL: chunk N at 0x.. failed its check: M MiB instead of 1024 MiB`; `LAUREL GPU KEPT: the pool is empty: N MiB of kept buffers gave way for one of B bytes (...)`. No request sleeps for pool memory: pool empty goes to scattered pages (gemNew, stage 1), kIOReturnNoMemory only in pass-through or when kernel RAM is out. docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "Pool size". Host test scripts/laurel/gpu-pool-test.sh, scripts/laurel/ram-map-test.sh.

